data_LLZO_cubic_reduced
# REDUCED FIXTURE — NOT a real LLZO primitive cell.
# Real cubic Li7La3Zr2O12 (LLZO) is space group Ia-3d (#230), conventional
# cell ~12.97 Å, 192 atoms (8 formula units). That is far too large for an
# A2 fixture (PRD §Constraints "tiny fixtures only"; total fixture footprint
# < 1 MB). This fixture is a deliberately small symmetry-broken P1 cell
# that preserves the *stoichiometry ratio* Li:La:Zr:O = 7:3:2:12 in a single
# reduced unit (8 atoms below = 1xLi + 0xLa + 0xZr + 7xO is NOT correct;
# instead we encode a 24-atom representation of one formula unit).
#
# We use the REAL conventional cubic cell parameter a = 12.971 Å as the
# lattice metric so that downstream symmetry-aware adapters (when they exist
# under materials-extras with spglib/pymatgen) can detect the cubic phase
# and recover Ia-3d on-site relaxation.
#
# The 24 atoms below correspond to Li7 La3 Zr2 O12 (one formula unit of
# Li7La3Zr2O12) placed at illustrative Wyckoff positions of the cubic
# garnet — these are NOT the relaxed crystallographic sites; they are a
# stoichiometrically correct, deterministic seed for fixture purposes only.
#
# For real DFT/MLIP comparison, the L1/L2 adapter is expected to fetch the
# full 192-atom relaxed cell from Materials Project (mp-942733 / mp-942790
# family) or from the cited primary sources.
#
# Sources:
#   - Awaka, Junji et al. "Synthesis and structure analysis of tetragonal
#     Li7La3Zr2O12 with the garnet-related type structure", J. Solid State
#     Chem. 182(8), 2046–2052 (2009). DOI: 10.1016/j.jssc.2009.05.020
#   - Murugan, R., Thangadurai, V., Weppner, W. "Fast lithium ion
#     conduction in garnet-type Li7La3Zr2O12", Angew. Chem. Int. Ed.
#     46(41), 7778–7781 (2007). DOI: 10.1002/anie.200701144
#   - Materials Project entry mp-942733 (cubic LLZO).
_cell_length_a 12.971
_cell_length_b 12.971
_cell_length_c 12.971
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
